^"owner_claim"{
 claim_id = "plan-mobile_runtime_foundation-001"
 layer = "pragmatic"
 hypothesis = `The desired end state is a site runtime that treats mobile and coarse-pointer use as the primary case rather than a degraded desktop fallback. The immediate task is not to ship new chrome, but to formalize the implementation surface: page regions with ownership, portable interaction semantics that do not depend on hover, complete operator interaction meanings, inspectable registers that back navigator/console projections, semantic HTML structures that act as the canonical reflection surface, and a clean preparation layer for future Spw blocks and scripts as UI. The longer arc is a cognitive machine that can produce wonder without becoming noisy: structure should become more legible as the user engages it, Spw symmetry should remain checkable across modalities, charge/bias metaphysics should be inspectable rather than hidden, and future Spw-backed components/pages should inherit that same ecosystem rather than bypass it. The taste note is clarity + containment: preserve the site's calm surface while making its deeper machinery easier to reason about, inspect, and extend.`
 spec_ref = ~"./PLAN.md"
 impl_ref = ~"../../../.agents/plans/mobile-runtime-foundation/mobile-runtime-foundation.spw"
 probe_ref = `Hypotheses: a shared region/register model will reduce runtime duplication; complete operator interaction semantics will prevent decorative grammar; portable inspect/invoke semantics will make mobile behavior easier to teach; prefix/postfix symmetry will let keyboard and touch feel like different entrances into the same grammar; semantic reflection into native HTML structures will keep the runtime honest across modalities; inspectable charge and bias can make brace physics useful without hidden state; recursive/fractal surface geometry can improve learnability if the same boundary/inspect/pivot pattern repeats across scales; block/script UI can be prepared without running the full language runtime in-browser.`
 falsification = `A patch cannot satisfy the public goal while leaving ../../../.agents/plans/mobile-runtime-foundation/mobile-runtime-foundation.spw unchanged or untested.`
 status = "active"
}[reg=facet]

scope: .{
 in = #[
  `In scope: define a page-region model, portable interaction semantics, complete operator interaction semantics, shared register/runtime boundaries, inspectability rules, UX constraints for an effective cognitive machine, prefix/postfix and reflection symmetry rules, HTML accessibility structures as semantic mirrors, recursive/fractal surface geometry as a structural model, brace-physics, charge/bias projection semantics, pivot semantics, no-dead-end exploration rules, and future-facing block/script host contracts; predict the runtime files and markup surfaces likely to change when implementation begins.`,
 ][reg=set]
 out = #[
  `: shipping the full spell system now, running the Spw parser in the browser, redesigning page aesthetics, or implementing block/script execution in this pass.`,
 ][reg=set]
}[reg=facet]

validation: #[
 `Hypotheses: a shared region/register model will reduce runtime duplication; complete operator interaction semantics will prevent decorative grammar; portable inspect/invoke semantics will make mobile behavior easier to teach; prefix/postfix symmetry will let keyboard and touch feel like different entrances into the same grammar; semantic reflection into native HTML structures will keep the runtime honest across modalities; inspectable charge and bias can make brace physics useful without hidden state; recursive/fractal surface geometry can improve learnability if the same boundary/inspect/pivot pattern repeats across scales; block/script UI can be prepared without running the full language runtime in-browser.`,
 `Negative controls: route structure, current visual voice, and basic static-site simplicity remain intact.`,
 `Demo sequence: identify the active region on mobile, inspect a component without hover, invoke the same component with touch or keyboard, pivot into a deeper surface without losing orientation, and confirm navigator/console can describe the same underlying register state.`,
][reg=set]

